// An integer-literal argument that does NOT fit the parameter type is rejected
// (it would silently truncate: 300 -> 44 in a u8). Literals that DO fit (e.g.
// `cf_take_u8(91)`) are accepted, since they materialize as a correct constant -
// that path is exercised throughout the stdlib.
//
// Reported as E0010 rather than E0214 once a numeric literal argument began
// adopting the PARAMETER's type: the literal IS a `u8`, so its width bound is
// checked where it is written and the diagnostic names the literal instead of
// reporting a mismatch at the call boundary. The rejection is what this case
// exists to pin; the file keeps its original name so the history stays in one
// place.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0010)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::E0214ArgLiteralOverflow;

function cf_take_u8(v: u8) -> void {}

function main() -> int {
    cf_take_u8(300);   //~ ERROR[E0010] out of range
    return 0;
}
